==================================================
1. CORE GAMEPLAY
==================================================
Teams: HIDERS vs SEEKERS. Up to 20 players per room (10 hiders, 10 seekers). Smaller rooms
(4-12) must work well; scale map zones and prop density to player count.

Hider character: a plain WHITE low-poly humanoid. Hiders must paint their own body to match the
surroundings and strike a pose that fits the spot. Unpainted white areas (elbows, hands,
backs of legs) are the classic way to get caught.

Round flow:
1. LOBBY: ready up, pick a map vote, customize name/outfit shape (body type only, not color).
2. PREP PHASE (75s, configurable): hiders explore, choose a spot, paint, and pose. Seekers
   wait in a sealed spawn room with a countdown and cannot see the map.
3. SEEK PHASE (5 min, configurable): seekers are released with guns and hunt. Hiders must
   stay perfectly still to keep their camouflage; moving breaks it (see rules below).
4. RESULTS: scoreboard, MVP highlights, replay-moment screenshot, return to lobby.

Hider rules:
- Painting is locked when prep ends (cannot repaint during seek phase).
- POSE WHEEL: 12 to 15 preset poses (stand, lean on wall, crouch ball, flat on floor, arms
  up, side profile, hug a pillar, T-pose, etc.), plus a limited "adjust limbs" mode later.
- LOCK-IN: pressing a key freezes the pose. Moving while seekers are within line of sight
  makes the hider "shimmer" (a subtle outline) visible to seekers for 2 seconds.
- Scoring: hiders earn points every second they are inside a seeker's field of view
  (within 15 m, unobstructed) without being shot. This rewards bold hiding in plain sight.
- Survival bonus if alive when the timer ends.

Seeker rules:
- Gun: hitscan, limited ammo (e.g., 12) with slow reload and a short cooldown.
- Hitting a hider eliminates them. Shooting at a non-hider costs a penalty (lose ammo, a brief
  slow, or a few HP; make it configurable) so spraying is not viable.
- Seekers earn points per elimination and for "first spot" assists (pinging a hider for
  teammates, which still requires a shot to eliminate).
- Eliminated hiders become spectators with a free-fly camera and a spectator-only voice channel.

Optional game modes (design them, implement later):
- Tag Mode (no guns, touch to catch), Chaos Mode (everyone hears everyone nearby),
  Streamer Mode (viewers vote on twists), Speed Round (30 s prep).

