4. MIC / VOICE COMMUNICATION
==================================================
Provider: LiveKit (FastAPI mints tokens). All channel rules are enforced SERVER-SIDE through
subscription permissions; never trust clients.

Channels by phase:
- LOBBY / RESULTS: everyone hears everyone (open).
- PREP PHASE: hiders hear hiders (full team), seekers hear seekers; no cross-team audio.
- SEEK PHASE:
    * Hiders: PROXIMITY voice only among hiders, 3D spatial audio, falloff to silence at
      ~15 m. Walls muffle sound with a low-pass filter.
    * Seekers: team radio, all seekers hear each other (optional proximity toggle).
    * Cross-team: seekers do NOT hear hiders directly. Instead, hider speech creates a
      NOISE EVENT computed server-side (hidden LiveKit participant reads active-speaker
      and audio levels). Louder speech means a larger, fuzzier ping direction on the
      seeker HUD plus a faint muffled spatial sound within ~10 m.
- SPECTATORS: their own channel; living players never hear them.

Room voice-rule presets (host chooses before the round, shown in the lobby):
- FAIR (default): rules above.
- CHAOS: everyone hears everyone in proximity, so hiders near seekers can be heard directly.
- SILENT HIDERS: hiders cannot speak after prep ends; seekers keep radio.
- STREAMER: viewers are muted by default; the host can unmute selected viewers.

Controls and safety:
- Voice listening is OFF/muted by default for new users with a clear prompt to enable it;
  push-to-talk as default key (V) with an open-mic option.
- Visible mic icon at the top of the screen when transmitting, and a speaking indicator
  above players' nameplates only for allowed audiences.
- Options: disable voice entirely, per-player mute and volume, block, and a "mute all".
- Report button that stores the last 30 seconds metadata (who, when, which room) for
  moderators; do not record audio without explicit legal and consent design.
- Moderators and hosts can mute or kick. Auto-mute players after repeated reports.
- Minimum age and a safety notice in the terms; clear microphone permission and HTTPS
  handling with friendly error messages.

